+    "content_html": "<p>The Numrexo Calorie Burn Calculator helps you estimate how many calories you burn while walking, running, cycling, swimming, or working out. Tracking your energy expenditure is an essential step toward achieving your fitness, weight loss, or maintenance goals.<br>Simply enter your body weight, choose your physical activity, and add your exercise duration to calculate your estimated calorie burn instantly.</p>\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>How Does the Calorie Burn Calculator Work?<br></strong></h2>\n\n<p>Our calculator estimates calories burned based on key physiological and workout factors:<br>Body weight: Heavier individuals naturally burn more calories performing the same movement because the body expends more energy to move mass.<br>Physical activity: Different activities require different amounts of energy based on their Metabolic Equivalent of Task (MET) value.<br>Exercise duration: The longer you sustain an activity, the higher your total caloric burn.<br>Activity intensity: High-intensity running or fast cycling burns significantly more calories per minute than moderate walking.</p>\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><br><strong>Step-by-Step: How to Use the Calculator?<br></strong></h2>\n\n<p>Using the Numrexo tool takes less than 30 seconds:<br>Enter Your Weight: Type your current body weight in kilograms (kg).<br>Select Your Activity: Choose your workout from the dropdown menu (e.g., walking, running, cycling).<br>Enter Duration: Input the total minutes spent exercising.<br>Click Calculate: Hit the calculate button to see your result.<br>View Results: Instantly view your total estimated calories burned.<br><strong><br></strong>Tracking your exercise burn provides helpful insights for your overall fitness journey:<br>Manage Calorie Deficit or Surplus: If your goal is weight loss, knowing your burn helps you balance energy in versus energy out alongside your daily diet.<br>Compare Workout Efficiency: Evaluate which exercises give you the best results in the time you have available.<br>Stay Motivated: Watching your numbers add up helps build consistency in your daily workout routine.<br>Note: Calorie calculators provide close estimates based on standardized averages. Your individual metabolic rate, age, gender, and muscle mass may cause slight variations.</p>\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><br><strong><strong><strong> </strong></strong>Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ) ?</strong></h2>\n\n<p><strong><br></strong>How many calories do you burn walking for 30 minutes?<br>On average, a person weighing 65\u201370 kg burns roughly 120 to 150 calories during a 30-minute moderate-paced walk. Use our calculator above with your exact weight for a personalized number.<br>Does running burn more calories than walking?<br>Yes. Running elevates your heart rate and engages larger muscle groups at higher intensities, burning nearly double the calories of walking over the same timeframe.<br>How accurate is an online calorie burn calculator?<br>While standard MET formulas provide reliable baselines, external factors such as terrain, resting metabolic rate, and workout intensity mean the result serves as an effective benchmark rather than a lab-exact measurement.<br></p>",
