+    "content_html": "<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n\n<h1 class=\"wp-block-heading\"></h1>\n\n<p>The moment a pregnancy test confirms positive, the most anticipated question is: \"When will my baby arrive?\"</p>\n\n<p>A standard full-term pregnancy lasts approximately 40 weeks (280 days) from the first day of your last period. While babies rarely arrive on an exact schedule, establishing an Estimated Due Date (EDD) is essential for tracking fetal development, scheduling prenatal screenings, and planning for labor.</p>\n\n<p>The Numrexo online Pregnancy Due Date Calculator eliminates manual date counting, delivering an accurate estimate based on clinically verified obstetric guidelines.</p>\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">How Is a Due Date Calculated? (Naegele\u2019s Rule)</h2>\n\n<p>Healthcare providers calculate delivery dates using Naegele\u2019s Rule, a standard clinical formula designed for an average 28-day menstrual cycle:</p>\n\n<ol class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Identify the first day of your Last Menstrual Period (LMP).</li>\n\n<li>Add 1 calendar year to that date.</li>\n\n<li>Subtract 3 months.</li>\n\n<li>Add 7 days.</li>\n</ol>\n\n<p>Clinical Formula:<br>Estimated Due Date (EDD) = First Day of LMP + 1 Year - 3 Months + 7 Days</p>\n\n<p>Calculation Example:</p>\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>First day of LMP: May 10, 2026</li>\n\n<li>Add 1 year: May 10, 2027</li>\n\n<li>Subtract 3 months: February 10, 2027</li>\n\n<li>Add 7 days: February 17, 2027 (Estimated Due Date)</li>\n</ul>\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">3 Reliable Ways to Determine Your Due Date</h2>\n\n<p>Depending on the regularity of your cycle and medical records, delivery dates are determined through one of three primary methods:</p>\n\n<ol class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Last Menstrual Period (LMP) Method:<br>This is the most common metric. Because ovulation typically occurs roughly 14 days after the start of a period, the 40-week timeline starts from cycle day 1, meaning you are technically considered \"two weeks pregnant\" at conception.</li>\n\n<li>Conception Date Method:<br>For individuals tracking basal body temperature, using ovulation predictor kits, or undergoing assisted reproductive technology (like IVF), the conception date may be precisely known. In this case, add 266 days (38 weeks) directly to the date of conception.</li>\n\n<li>Early Ultrasound Dating Scan:<br>If menstrual cycles are irregular, an ultrasound scan performed during the first trimester (weeks 7\u201312) provides the most reliable date. Technicians measure the baby\u2019s Crown-Rump Length (CRL) to estimate gestational age within an accuracy window of 3 to 5 days.</li>\n</ol>\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">The 3 Trimesters of Pregnancy</h2>\n\n<p>A 40-week pregnancy is divided into three functional stages called trimesters, each marked by critical developmental milestones:</p>\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>First Trimester (Week 1 to Week 12): Rapid cell differentiation, organ formation, detection of heartbeat.</li>\n\n<li>Second Trimester (Week 13 to Week 26): Fetal movements (quickening), gender identification via anatomy scan, bone ossification.</li>\n\n<li>Third Trimester (Week 27 to Delivery): Rapid lung maturation, fat deposition, baby shifts into vertex (head-down) position.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Do Babies Arrive Exactly on Their Due Date?</h2>\n\n<p>Only about 4% to 5% of babies are born precisely on their estimated due date.</p>\n\n<p>The due date serves as a central reference point rather than an absolute deadline. A pregnancy is clinically categorized as:</p>\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Early Term: 37 weeks 0 days to 38 weeks 6 days</li>\n\n<li>Full Term: 39 weeks 0 days to 40 weeks 6 days</li>\n\n<li>Late Term: 41 weeks 0 days to 41 weeks 6 days</li>\n\n<li>Postterm: 42 weeks 0 days and beyond</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>Delivery anytime between 37 and 42 weeks is normal and expected for a healthy pregnancy.</p>\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Why Use the Numrexo Due Date Calculator?</h2>\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Instant Clinical Accuracy: Built directly on Naegele\u2019s standard obstetric algorithm to avoid manual calendar errors.</li>\n\n<li>Cycle-Length Flexibility: Accommodates non-standard cycle lengths for more personalized estimation.</li>\n\n<li>Milestone Planning: Helps align prenatal appointments, routine blood panels, and leave preparation with your current gestational week.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>To find your delivery window, enter the first day of your last period into the Numrexo calculator above to generate your customized pregnancy timeline.</p>\n\n<p></p>",
